'' The runtime inventory. docs/plan/11 section 3: no 'fb_StrAssign' string literal
'' anywhere else in tiko-lang, so that there is ONE place to audit against the runtime and
'' a dumpable list that can be diffed against the library's real exports.
''
'' The full differential -- return type, arity and every parameter type, plus a
'' cross-check that each name is an exported symbol of libfb.a -- is
'' tools/gen/check-rtl.sh, which needs fbc present. This is the part that does not.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-rtl tests/rtl/src/empty.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrAssign ptr (ptr, i64, ptr, i64, i32)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrDelete void (ptr)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrCompare i32 (ptr, i64, ptr, i64)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ArrayRedimEx i32 (ptr, i64, i32, i32, i64, ...)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ThreadCreate ptr (ptr, ptr, i64)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrAssignMid void (ptr, i64, i64, ptr)
'' fb_UStrToStr is the 520th: 'val( <ustring> )' converts through it (tests/mir/val-ustring).
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_UStrToStr ptr (ptr, i64)
'' AND FOUR MORE FOR THE NON-LOCAL ERROR JUMP, 2026-09-20. 'ON ERROR GOTO' installs a
'' handler in one procedure and the throw may be in another; LLVM cannot branch across
'' functions, so the compiler setjmps where the handler is installed and the runtime
'' longjmps into it. Two of the four are the C library's own setjmp under the two names
'' it has: tiko links ucrtbase, which exports '__intrinsic_setjmp' and not '_setjmp'.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ErrorJmpBuf ptr ()
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ErrorGetHandler ptr ()
'' EXPECT-OUT: rtl: 525 entries
